00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Honor Was Their Code.

2
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Windtalkers is a war, action film directed by John Woo.

3
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Joe Enders is a gung-ho Marine assigned to protect a "windtalker" - one of several Navajo Indians who were used to relay
messages during World War II because their spoken language was indecipherable to Japanese code breakers.

4
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Sergeant Joe Enders, played by Nicolas Cage.

5
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:46,000
Private Ben Yahzee, played by Adam Beach.

6
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:42,000
Sergeant Eric Hjelmstad, played by Peter Stormare.

7
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:38,000
Corporal Charles Rogers, played by Noah Emmerich.

8
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:34,000
Pappas, played by Mark Ruffalo.

9
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:30,000
Harrigan, played by Brian Van Holt.

10
01:29:20,000 --> 01:29:26,000
Windtalkers is a 2002 American war film directed and co-produced by John Woo, starring Nicolas Cage and Adam
Beach, with Peter Stormare, Noah Emmerich, Mark Ruffalo, and Christian Slater in supporting roles.

11
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:22,000
It is based on the real story of code talkers from
the Navajo nation during World War II.

12
01:47:12,000 --> 01:47:18,000
The film was theatrically released in the United States by MGM Distribution Co.

13
01:56:08,000 --> 01:56:14,000
on June 14, 2002, receiving mixed-to-negative reviews from critics and grossing just $76.7 million
worldwide against a production budget of $115 million, making it a box-office bomb.

14
02:05:04,000 --> 02:05:10,000
The film explores themes of japan, world war ii, radio
transmission, marine corps, us army.
